-- title:
--   Degeneracy inclusion is compatible with the two class-set dictionaries
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of prime characteristic $q'$ which is algebraic over $\mathbb{Z}/q'$, and let $X_1$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ all of whose $q'$-torsion is trivial (every $P$ with $q'\cdot P=0$ vanishes). Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q'`, i.e. $a<0$, $b<0$ and, for each height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra precisely when $q'\in v$; let $\Lambda_1$ be a maximal order (an order, maximal among orders containing it) and $\theta_1$ an injective ring homomorphism from the subring of rational endomorphisms of $X_1$ onto $\Lambda_1$. Let $N\neq 0$ with $q'\nmid N$, and let $m$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ with $m$ and $N\,m^{-1}$ in the adelic box of $\Lambda_1$ (the group generated by the $z\otimes a$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$ and $a$ an integral adele), with $\Lambda_1$ conjugated by $m$ again maximal, and set $R=\Lambda_1\cap m\Lambda_1 m^{-1}$, assumed of relative index $N$ in $\Lambda_1$. Let $q$ be a prime with $q\nmid N$ and $q'\nmid Nq$, and let $m'$ satisfy the same conditions at level $Nq$ ($m'$ and $(Nq)\,m'^{-1}$ in the box, the conjugate order maximal, $S=\Lambda_1\cap m'\Lambda_1 m'^{-1}$ of relative index $Nq$), together with the compatibilities $m^{-1}m'$ and $q\,m'^{-1}m$ in the box. Let $e_V$ be a bijection from the double coset set $\mathbb{H}^\times\backslash\widehat{\mathbb{H}}^\times/\mathrm{Stab}(\widehat R)$ onto the supersingular places `ssPlaces q' N κ` — the rational, affine-geometric places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ N` whose value at `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q'` — and let $e_E$ be such a bijection at level $Nq$ for $S$. Assume $e_V$ is pinned to moduli places in the following sense: for all $x$, all elliptic $W$ and nonzero $\chi\colon X_1\to W$ in the rational hom set, all units $d$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ with $\theta_1$ of the kernel-ideal set of $\chi$ equal to the image under quaternion conjugation of $d\cdot\Lambda_1 x$, all elliptic $W'$ and rational $\psi\colon W\to W'$ admitting a rational $\psi'$ with $\psi'\circ\psi=N$ and $\psi\circ\psi'=N$ and with $\theta_1$ of the kernel-ideal set of $\psi\circ\chi$ the conjugate image of $d\cdot\Lambda_1(xm)$, and with $\ker\psi$ cyclic of order $N$: the valuation subring of $e_V([x]_R)$ is the preimage of that of `moduliPlace κ N W ψ.ker` under the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldC κ N` into the full modular function field. Assume the analogous hypothesis for $e_E$ at level $Nq$ (with $m'$ in place of $m$). Finally assume $j_{q,N}\in$ `modularFunctionFieldC κ (N*q)`, so that the degeneracy inclusion `levelAlphaC κ N q` of `modularFunctionFieldC κ N` into `modularFunctionFieldC κ (N*q)` is defined, and assume this inclusion is integral. Then for every finite idele unit $x$, restricting the place $e_E([x]_S)$ along this inclusion — pulling back its valuation subring — gives exactly $e_V([x]_R)$.
--
--   This is the degeneracy-map compatibility of the Deuring–Eichler dictionary between quaternionic class sets and supersingular points: passing from level $Nq$ to level $N$ by forgetting the $q$-part of the level structure corresponds, on class sets, to the identity on representatives. It feeds the construction of the commuting square of degeneracy and Hecke data in [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_equiv_classSet_ssPlaces_degeneracy_hecke_comm`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_equiv_classSet_ssPlaces_degeneracy_hecke_comm).
